		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3900&amp;p=30284#p30284"><![CDATA[
I'm new to OpenGD77 on a new TYT MD-UV390 and am loving the combination.  However, I did accidentally pressed SK2 while powering on and of course reset the FW and so all the radio settings.  That's when it dawned on me that there's nowhere in the CPS where radio settings are stored.  Am I missing something or is there another way to save the radio settings (display, sound, etc.)?  If not, is the OpenGD77 team planning on including that cape bility at some point in the future so we can backup the radio settings?<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5794">W3ATN</a> — Fri Mar 22, 2024 2:11 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
